HMM Regime Trading System — Implementation Plan
Context
The PixityAI per-symbol swing/reversion strategy was invalidated by Phase 6 scan: only 4/196 symbols passed walk-forward validation, with tiny returns (0.3-2.6% over 7 months). The old "86 profitable" result was an artifact of 3 compounding bugs (position stacking, no tracking, look-ahead bias).

This plan implements a fundamentally different approach: a macro regime-based system that classifies the market state daily using an HMM on intermarket features, then trades Nifty 50 index directionally and filters equity entries by regime. The edge is avoiding bad trades in chop markets, not predicting winning ones.

Architecture

Layer 1: OBSERVER  (daily features from VIX, BankNifty, USDINR, Nifty)
                |
Layer 2: CLASSIFIER  (HMM -> state probabilities: Expansion/Contraction/Shock)
                |
Layer 3: EXECUTOR  (intraday 15m strategy: regime gate + technical confirmation)
                |
        Existing Infrastructure  (TradingRunner -> ExecutionHandler -> PaperBroker)
Key decisions:

Daily HMM classification at market open, intraday 15m execution
Nifty 50 cash index as proxy + regime-filtered equities
Fresh module alongside existing code, reusing runner/handler/backtest infra
No Brent crude for now; Bank Nifty, India VIX, USDINR via Upstox
