Phase 2: Classifier Module (HMM)
File: core/strategies/regime/classifier.py
New dependency: hmmlearn


class HMMRegimeClassifier:
    def fit(self, features: pd.DataFrame) -> None
    def predict_proba(self, features: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame  # P(state) per day
    def classify(self, features_row, date) -> RegimeClassification
    def save(path) / load(path)  # joblib serialization
Training: StandardScaler -> GaussianHMM(n_states=3, covariance_type='full', n_iter=200)

Training window: Test 6, 9, and 12-month windows. 6 months (~120 obs) is tight for 3-state full covariance — prefer 9-12 months if data permits. Compare state stability across window sizes.

State mapping (rank-based scoring, NOT position-based):


# Rank states by composite score instead of assuming VIX ordering
shock_score = rank(vix_mean) + rank(realized_vol_mean)
expansion_score = -rank(vix_mean) + rank(nifty_slope_mean)
# Assign labels by highest composite score per state
This avoids fragile assumptions about which state has "lowest" VIX.

Override rules (bypass HMM in extreme conditions):

VIX 90d percentile > 85% AND USDINR slope > 0 -> force SHOCK
VIX 5-day RoC > 20% -> force SHOCK
Regime stability metric: Track state entropy H = -sum(p * log(p)). High entropy = unclear regime -> reduce position size proportionally.

Output: State probabilities (not discrete) — P(Expansion), P(Contraction), P(Shock)

Phase 3: Executor Module
3a. Strategy (core/strategies/regime/executor.py)
Extends BaseStrategy.process_bar(). Daily regime cached, intraday signals on 15m bars.

Trading logic:

P(Expansion) > 0.70 for 2 consecutive days + technical confirmation -> LONG entry
P(Shock) > 0.65 or P(Contraction) > 0.65 -> EXIT longs
High entropy (unclear regime) -> reduce position size by 50%
Otherwise -> NO TRADE (preserve capital)
Regime persistence filter: Require threshold exceeded for 2 consecutive days before acting. Prevents one-day false spikes and flip-flopping.

Intraday entry confirmation (15m):

EMA(9) > EMA(21) crossover
Volume z-score > 1.0
Price above session VWAP
ATR-based SL (1.5x ATR) and TP (2.0x ATR)
Batch mode: For backtesting, batch_generate_regime_signals() generates all signals vectorized upfront -> feeds through PrecomputedSignalStrategy (same pattern as PixityAI batch).

3b. Sizing (core/strategies/regime/sizing.py)
Volatility parity: Position Size = (0.75% of capital) / (2 * ATR)
Weekly risk cap = 3%

3c. Circuit Breaker (core/strategies/regime/circuit_breaker.py)
Weekly drawdown > 3% -> halt all trading until next Monday.

