Phase 5: Validation
MANDATORY: HMM vs simple VIX threshold — does HMM add value over VIX < 15 = expansion, VIX > 22 = shock? If not, use the simpler model.
State count optimization: Compare 2/3/4 states via out-of-sample Sharpe
Training window comparison: 6 vs 9 vs 12 months — check state mean stability
Threshold sensitivity: Test P(Expansion) at 0.60, 0.65, 0.70, 0.75, 0.80
Baseline comparisons: HMM vs rule-based RegimeDetector vs GMM vs buy-and-hold
Regime accuracy check: Do expansion days actually contain majority of positive Nifty returns? Do shock days contain crash clusters? If distribution is random, HMM has no edge.
Trade frequency monitor: If expansion regime produces <2 trades/week, intraday filter is too tight — relax confirmation
Regime visualization: Nifty chart with color-coded regime overlay + state probability time series
